  "StockRole": "Unknown",
  "YangsThoughts": "Why did they remove an arm? WHY does the other arm only have a shoulder, and for some clownish reason a HAND bolted directly onto it!? That's not how arms work! Who approved this?! Who looked at this thing and thought, 'Yes, that's a perfectly reasonable weapons platform'?! And what did the pilot mean when he wrote 'I went to a Mapleton's and the coffee was bad' in the maintenance log? Is that supposed to be a warning? A distress signal? Some kind of Quicsell corporate code? I'm not investigating this anymore",
